1548	+/// The chat feature's one port — `features/chat/presentation` depends on
1549	+/// this abstract class only, never `chat/data` (RNF06). Every method but
1550	+/// [sendMessage] returns `Future<Either<Failure, T>>` (RNF09); [sendMessage]
1551	+/// alone returns a `Stream` given the SSE nature of its response
1552	+/// (Boundaries).
1553	+abstract class ChatRepository {
1554	+  /// Calls `chat-sessions-list` (`ApiClient.get`, via
1555	+  /// `ChatRemoteDataSource`) — works offline via the `chat_sessions` Hive
1556	+  /// box (Code Map): on [Failure.networkOffline]/[Failure.networkTimeout],
1557	+  /// falls back to a full dump of that box, same "cache fallback"
1558	+  /// convention `EntriesRepositoryImpl.list()` already uses for its own
1559	+  /// first/fresh page. Every other [Failure] propagates as `Left`,
1560	+  /// unmapped (RNF09).
1561	+  Future<Either<Failure, List<ChatSession>>> listSessions();
1562	+
1563	+  /// Calls `chat-sessions-create` (`ApiClient.post`) with no title
1564	+  /// (Boundaries: "`chat-sessions-create` with no title") — blocked
1565	+  /// offline per `requirements.md` ("`POST /chat/sessions` — blocked
1566	+  /// offline"), so unlike [listSessions] there is no cache fallback here:
1567	+  /// every [Failure], including [Failure.networkOffline], is returned as
1568	+  /// `Left`, unmapped. On success, persists the new session to the
1569	+  /// `chat_sessions` Hive box before returning `Right`, same
1570	+  /// "persist then return" ordering [listSessions] already uses.
1571	+  Future<Either<Failure, ChatSession>> createSession();
1572	+
1573	+  /// Calls `chat-messages-list` (`ApiClient.get`, [sessionId] appended as
1574	+  /// the one trailing path segment) — works offline via the
1575	+  /// `chat_messages` Hive box, same cache-fallback convention
1576	+  /// [listSessions] already uses, filtered to [sessionId] and sorted by
1577	+  /// `seq` ascending (the backend's own "ordered by seq", `openapi.yaml`).
1578	+  Future<Either<Failure, List<ChatMessage>>> listMessages(String sessionId);
1579	+
1580	+  /// Calls `chat-messages-send` (`ApiClient.postStream`, [sessionId]
1581	+  /// appended as the one trailing path segment) with `{content}` — the
1582	+  /// one streaming exception to this port's otherwise all-`Future` shape
1583	+  /// (Boundaries/RNF09: "every other method returns
1584	+  /// `Future<Either<Failure, T>>`"). No connectivity resolves immediately
1585	+  /// to a single `Left(Failure.networkOffline)` emission, never queued
1586	+  /// (Boundaries) — `ApiClient.postStream`'s own first awaited `Dio.post`
1587	+  /// call surfaces that failure before any byte streams. A connection that
1588	+  /// closes without a `done`/`error` SSE event is surfaced as a single
1589	+  /// trailing `Left(Failure.networkTimeout)` (Design Notes: "the taxonomy
1590	+  /// has no dedicated 'dropped stream' code"). No local write queue, no
1591	+  /// Hive persistence of sent messages (Design Notes: chat holds no local
1592	+  /// write queue for this story).
